{
  "name": "Camera (Android CamX HAL through a bridge) - EXPERIMENTAL",
  "default": true,
  "description": "sweet's camera sensors, ISP and JPEG encoder only work through Qualcomm's Android camera HAL (CamX, camera.qcom.so). sweetcam-launch runs it in a private mount namespace that looks like a minimal Android (/system, /vendor, /apex from /vendor/android, an Android property area) inside cambridge, a small bionic program that drives the camera3 HAL and hands the frames over a unix socket. sweet_camera_host implements the OpenHarmony camera HDI (v1.0), registers camera_service with the HDF service manager like Huawei's CameraDaemon and copies the frames into the apps' buffer queues (preview NV21/NV12, JPEG photos). The camera libraries, tuning files and ICP firmware come from the sweet ROM; the bionic runtime and the few AOSP libraries it needs are shipped here. Logs: /data/log/sweetcam and 'cambridge:'/'sweet-camera:' lines in kmsg.",
